- * Instead the queue gets an eventfd that only the PMD writes:
- * rtl_dev_interrupt_handler() writes it when an interrupt arrives while the
- * queue is armed. The interrupt is one-shot: the handler masks the RX causes
- * again and rx_queue_intr_enable() re-arms them. max_intr stays 0, so vfio
- * still enables only the first MSI-X vector and never sees this eventfd.
- *
